  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Sustainable and State-Led Interventions in Support to the Transition in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The transition to a state-led migration response in Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) is an important process supported by the European Union, International Organization for Migration and BiH authorities since 2021. Several milestones have been reached in recent years to progressively transfer the ownership of the migration response and the temporary reception centers to relevant state institutions. In support of the BiH Strategy on Migration and Asylum 2021-2025 and the upcoming launch of a tripartite Working Group including the Ministry of Security, the Ministry of Civil Affairs and the Ministry for Human Rights and Refugees, BiH enters a new phase in the ongoing transition to a state-led migration response, where technical and human capacities of institutions will be critical to establish well-defined systems and structures for the long-term management of mixed movements in BiH. Through this intervention, IOM is contributing to this transition through supporting the consolidation of the roles and responsibilities of the MHRR and its main partner in the field, the National Red Cross Society of BiH, as well as the institution in charge of the management of temporary reception centres in BiH, the Service for Foreigners&#x2019; Affairs.</narrative>
  </description>
